# Never upload local secrets — production values live in Vercel's env settings.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Build/local artifacts
.next
node_modules
.claude

# Not needed by the build (raw design references, agent skills, QA harnesses)
design-exports
design-stitch
design-figma
skills
scripts/_qa-*
.probe-*.mjs

# ── THE ANDROID APP IS NOT PART OF THE WEB DEPLOY ────────────────────────────
# nivora_app/ is 1.1 GB (Flutter SDK caches, .dart_tool, build/, the AAR/APK tree) and the
# Next.js build does not read a single byte of it. Left in, the upload reached 568 MB and the
# deploy died — first as ECONNRESET against this machine's TLS-intercepting antivirus, then as
# a bare "Internal Server Error" from the archive endpoint. Nine days of production drift
# traced back to exactly this: deploys that could not finish.
#
# dist/ is the staged APK/AAB (127 MB) and android/ is a stale top-level Gradle tree. Same
# reasoning: neither is an input to `next build`.
nivora_app
dist
android
